  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "S1 imposes strict 24-hour serious-incident reporting, 5-business-day other reporting, and 72-hour customer notices. S2 sets a 55 °C/5% test limit but lets over-limit models continue marketing while they submit corrective-action plans and retest, with results to regulators and purchasers but no public per-model failure rates. S3 delays new-unit shut-off to 24 months and gives a 6-year retrofit window; S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months; S5 mandates recall above 8/100k with 72-hour notices and no transition."
